Feature: SQL-based logic for f_invntry_bal_dly_hist table

  Background:
    Given the Unity Catalog information is available
    And the schema is purgo_playground
    And the target table is f_invntry_bal_dly_hist

  Scenario Outline: Validate field mappings
    Given source-to-target mapping is defined in the data_map sheet
    When the mapping specifies <Source Column Name> from <Source Table Name>
    Then it should map to <Target Column Name> in f_invntry_bal_dly_hist
    And the datatype should convert from <Source Datatype> to <Target Datatype>
    And any logic specified as <Logic> should be applied

    Examples:
      | Source Table Name | Source Column Name | Source Datatype | Target Column Name | Target Datatype | Logic                  |
      | source_table_1    | src_col_1          | varchar         | target_col_1       | string          | UPPER(src_col_1)       |
      | source_table_2    | src_col_2          | int             | target_col_2       | bigint          |                       |

  Scenario: Successful data retrieval with filters
    Given data is sourced from purgo_playground.purgo_playground.d_product_hist
    When the filter 'flag_active = true' is applied
    Then only records with flag_active set to 1 are retrieved

  Scenario: Ensure proper join conditions
    Given tables from the Source sheet require joining
    When the join type specified is INNER JOIN
    And joining conditions are defined in the Joins sheet as "table1.id = table2.fk_id"
    Then ensure the SQL query concatenates this join accurately

  Scenario: Validate error condition for missing data
    Given a source column <missing_column> is not found in source data
    When attempting to map this column
    Then an error message "Column <missing_column> not found in source" should be produced

    Examples:
      | missing_column |
      | src_col_missing |

  Scenario: Error handling for datatype mismatch
    Given a mapping specifies datatype conversion from int to date
    When the source data is not compatible
    Then an error message "Datatype mismatch for column <int_column> expected DATE" is generated

    Examples:
      | int_column |
      | int_col_1  |

  Scenario: Data-driven test for various input scenarios
    Given the data mappings are defined correctly
    When various scenarios are tested
    Then ensure correct target data population for each scenario
    And verify no unexpected errors occur

    Examples:
      | scenario                  | input_value | expected_result               |
      | Missing mandatory field   | NULL        | "Mandatory field missing"     |
      | Incorrect date format     | 20201332    | "Invalid date format"         |
      | Correct data entry        | 20230101    | "Data populated successfully" |

